# 1. PRODUCT VISION

NayanSathi is an AI-powered, browser-based Augmentative and Alternative Communication (AAC) platform designed for people who cannot communicate effectively through speech or conventional physical interaction.

The application should allow users to control a computer interface using their eye movements through an ordinary webcam.

The user should be able to:

1. Move a cursor by looking at different areas of the screen.
2. Calibrate the system to their individual eye movements.
3. Select interface buttons using dwell-based selection.
4. Construct sentences without typing or speaking.
5. Communicate using text-to-speech.
6. Access intelligent, context-aware sentence suggestions.
7. Communicate in Hindi and English.
8. Send emergency messages.
9. Allow caregivers to personalize the communication experience.

The platform must be accessible, intuitive, responsive, reliable and privacy-conscious.

**Core principle:** A person should be able to communicate meaningful thoughts using only their eyes, without requiring a mouse, keyboard or touchscreen.

